// Steam's operations. Achievements and stats go by their API names (the text);
// set_stat and set_stat_float set `a`, add_stat adds `a` to an integer stat, and
// these and get_stat answer the stat's value. set_presence sets rich presence
// key (the text's first `a` code points) to the rest of the text; clear_presence
// clears every key. status answers ok while Steam runs for the game, unavailable
// otherwise. Steam Input: input_action_set activates the action set named by the
// text on every controller, input_glyph answers the path of the glyph image of
// the first button or stick bound to the action named by the text in the active
// set (a digital action, or an analog one), and input_panel opens Steam's
// binding panel, where the player rebinds them; each answers unavailable without
// Steam Input or a controller. The Workshop's: workshop_publish uploads the
// player's saved scene (the editor's) as an item titled with the text, visible
// to `a` (0 everyone, 1 friends, 2 only the player, 3 those with the link), or
// with `b` 1 as a new version of the item whose id is the text's first line,
// answered later with the item's id as text and value 1 when the player must
// accept the Workshop's agreement; workshop_items answers the installed
// subscribed items' ids as text, a space between them, their count the value,
// and downloads the rest; workshop_subscribe and workshop_unsubscribe take an
// item's id as text and answer once Steam has; workshop_use makes an installed
// item's scene the player's, for the game to load as the editor's scene.
