const pathfinding_op_find = 0

// The host's developer tools. log answers the log's lines from serial `a` on,
// value the serial after the last, each line as its source (0 game, 1 build, 2
// reload, 3 asset, 4 pipeline, 5 session), 1 if an error, its length and its
// code points. frame answers the last frame's numbers in DEVTOOLS_FRAME's order,
// timing the game's frames while `a` is 1. gpu answers the graphics adapter's
// name. command sends the game console command `a` with argument `b`. pause and
// play stop and start the game's clock; step runs `a` frames and stays paused;
// rewind goes back `a` seconds of game time, paused; replay plays the last `a`
// seconds again, then live; history keeps the past to travel in (unavailable
// answers what needs it while none is kept). record starts recording the input
// to the text's path, or a new file when it is empty, or stops a recording. shot
// saves the window with the dev tools over it to the text's path, or a new file.
// tune sets the live-tunable constant whose id is `a` to `b`, and tuned answers
// the game's tuned values as id and value pairs. bake writes them into the
// checkout as the defaults, or only the one whose id is `a` when `a` is not 0.
// packets keeps each frame's input and render packets from now on while `a` is 1
// (the last 120 frames), or forgets them at 0, and answers the frames kept,
// oldest first, each as DEVTOOLS_PACKET's numbers; packet_diff answers how frame
// `b` differs from frame `a`, both kept: for each of DEVTOOLS_PACKET's numbers
// after position, its count in `a`, its count in `b` and how many of its
// elements differ. state answers the live state's sections (`a` below 0), each
// its key, version, width and length, value the state's schema, or up to 256
// lanes of section `a` from lane `b` on, value its length; with `c` above 0, of
// the state the history kept `c` seconds of game time back instead. state_diff
// answers, for each section of the live state or the one kept `a` seconds back,
// its key, its length then and now, how many lanes differ and the first that
// does (-1 for none), value the frame compared with. pictures takes a picture of
// the game's frame each time the history could keep a moment, while `a` is 1,
// into the dev tools' atlas (the texture of material `b`: slots of 128 by 80
// pixels, 8 to a row, the first 16 for pictures), and answers each picture's
// slot and the frame that shows it, oldest first; seek goes to frame `a`,
// paused. watch pauses the game once lane `b` of the live state's section `a`
// compares with `d` as DEVTOOLS_COMPARE `c` says, `a` -1 stops watching and -2
// only asks; it answers the watch: key, lane, comparison, value, the lane's
// value now and the frame it paused at (-1 for none). profile samples the game's
// guest while `a` is 1, stops at 0 and forgets the samples at 2 (3 only asks),
// answering how many it has and 1 while sampling; flame answers them as a flame
// graph, value the samples: first how many functions follow that the samples
// found running most, each its function index, samples, its name's length and
// code points; then each node (a caller before its callees) as its depth,
// function index, first sample, samples, samples in it alone, its name's length
// and code points. memory answers the game's committed memory in bytes, the most
// it committed, then for each counter the guest exports (guest ABI 3's ownership
// counters) and the host's calls into it, its name's length, code points and
// value in two 24-bit halves, value the number of counters. presets answers the
// names of the checkout's tunable presets, a line each; preset_save saves the
// game's tuned values as the preset the text names, and preset_load tunes each
// value of that preset. assets answers the game's catalog of DEVTOOLS_ASSET `a`,
// each entry as its DEVTOOLS_ASSET_STATE, its revision, its key's length and
// code points. preview draws catalog asset `b` of kind `a` (a mesh with material
// `c`, a material on mesh `c`) into slot `d` (16 to 63) of the atlas pictures
// named, value 1 once drawn and 0 while its assets load. swap draws catalog
// asset `b` of kind `a` from the asset the text names instead, or its own again
// when the text is empty, until the next build. material answers material `a`'s
// color and instance parameters (8 numbers, 0 when it sets none), whether it
// sets them (two numbers), then its shader's and texture's names, each its
// length and code points; material_set sets number `b` of those 8 in the
// checkout's file to `c`, which then reloads. audit checks the game's interface
// as the last frame showed it and answers its findings: value their count, and
// for each its kind (AUDIT_FINDING_*), the node's id, a measure (a contrast
// ratio, a size in pixels, or 0), its message's length and the message's code
// points. audio answers the mix as it plays: DEVTOOLS_AUDIO's numbers, then
// DEVTOOLS_BUS's for each bus, the master first; peaks and RMS are linear and
// over what played since the last audio answer. mute silences bus `a` while `b`
// is 1 and solo hears only the soloed buses (and the master's own voices) while
// any is soloed; both are the developer's, never the game's or a recording's.
// export hands the game's state over as a save file named by the text, or a new
// one (the browser downloads it); import loads a save file the player hands over
// (the browser asks for one), or plays an input recording. systems measures
// named game systems while a is 1, stops at 0, and answers a bounded page
// starting at row b (64 rows maximum). Row zero refreshes the snapshot;
// subsequent pages read that same snapshot. Value is the total system count.
// Each row contains stage (Start through Settle, 0-6), id, calls since the
// previous snapshot, mean milliseconds, maximum milliseconds, execution mode (0
// sequential), mean requested allocation bytes per call, mean allocation count
// per call, name length and code points. Uncalled systems have -1 timings;
// allocation means are -1 without allocation instrumentation or calls.
// Unsupported hosts answer unavailable. semantic exchanges bounded JSON text for
// opt-in application descriptors, decoded object values, decision events,
// watches and exact timeline seeks; see docs/semantic-inspection.md for version
// 1, limits, pagination and explicit unavailable reasons.
